# HD-EMS project rules

## Context
Event-camera motion segmentation using Vector-Symbolic Architectures.
Read docs/SPEC.md before writing any code in hdems/vsa/.

## Hard constraints — do not violate
- FPE MUST be implemented as exp(1j * x * phases). NEVER ifft(fft(X)**x):
  complex powers have branch cuts and fail silently.
- Base vectors MUST be unitary (unit modulus in the phasor domain), otherwise
  unbinding is not the inverse of binding.
- Binding in the phasor domain is ELEMENTWISE PRODUCT, not torch.conv1d.
- The bundled-field window M must stay <= 9. Retrieval degrades sharply beyond
  this (measured). Extend range with pyramid levels, never with larger M.
- Do not "simplify" the two-pass separable field into an explicit M^2 loop.
  Separability is the entire efficiency contribution.

## Style
- Type hints everywhere. Tensor shapes in every docstring as (B, d, H, W).
- Complex tensors: torch.complex64. Assert dtype at module boundaries.
- No magic numbers. All constants come from configs/*.yaml.
- Every hdems/vsa/ function needs a unit test before it is used elsewhere.

## Testing
- pytest tests/ must pass before adding features.
- tests/test_field_exact.py and tests/test_retrieval.py are correctness gates.
  If they fail, STOP and report — do not adjust the thresholds to make them pass.
